I am informed by the C.B.C. as follows: (a) The C.B.C. owns a television rebroadcasting transmitter, CBVT-1, located adjacent to Highway 24, 2| miles northeast of St. George de Beauce; (b) 1967; (c) $56,227; (d) Work was carried out under supervision of C.B.C. engineers; (e) and (f) RCA Victor, transmission facilities:	$44,580; G. Morissette,
building: $3,400; improvements to property: $2,200; Land, legal fees, surveying: $4,144; Provincial sales tax: $1,903; (g) five watts;
(h)	Service is not omnidirectional hence there is no radius of service. St. George de Beauce is southwest of the transmitter and from south to northwest the estimated Grade A service is 3 miles; Grade B is eight miles;
(i)	C.B.C. engineering headquarters; (j) Approximately $2,000; (k) Further study by C.B.C. engineers shows that due to the terrain some areas receive an inadequate signal. An application has been submitted to the CRTC for the relocation of this station to overcome the problem while maintaining satisfactory service in those areas where the signal is now acceptable.
